#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""session-end: the mechanical half of ending a thread (pause, move or close).

  session-end <pause|move|close> [--repo PATH]... [--transcript FILE]
              [--wait SECONDS] [--dry-run] [--json]
  session-end finish [--logged N | --declined REASON] [--json]

Every ending starts with `session-end <mode>`. It snapshots git, starts the
repo cleanup (branch-gc), rebuilds this directory's memory index, lints when the
thread touched harness files, and prints what is left for the agent to decide.
It makes no judgment calls: it never commits, pushes, edits a ticket, logs
time, writes a baton, compacts, settles or deletes scratch. Its writes are the
selected repos' existing branch-gc mechanic, the resolved memory index, its own
receipt and GC run files, and (finish only) the closeout stamp and the archive
of this thread's billing stamps.

`finish` runs after the agent has saved lessons, fixed documents and written
the resume note. It reads this thread's receipt, re-reads a pending GC result,
and only when that run was real and nothing failed does it advance
<state>/last-closeout. After a close it requires exactly one of --logged N (N
time entries created and read back, 0 allowed) or --declined REASON, and
archives this thread's two billing stamp files.

Why one command: the
mechanical steps of the three endings lived as prose in three skills, and a
close assembled by hand skipped steps. Why `finish` is separate: clearing the
billing stamps inside the first call would erase the unbilled-window flag
before the time is logged, so a close that stopped halfway would lose the
evidence; and last-closeout is the lower bound of transcript knowledge mining,
so it must not move before knowledge capture is done.

Scope, stated in the output too:
  - Claude sessions only (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID). Under Codex or OpenCode the
    steps that need no transcript run for explicit --repo values; the
    transcript, time and billing steps print "unsupported provider", and
    finish archives nothing. The billing stamp's key helper has no Codex branch.
  - The main thread only. A T3-delegated lane (T3CODE_THREAD_ID starting
    thread:delegated-task: or thread:provider:, or `lane-class --self` saying
    t3-lane or agent-lane) is refused every writing mode; --dry-run stays open.
    An in-process helper shares its main thread's environment, so the Bash
    guard (hooks/git-guard.sh) blocks it from the payload's agent_id instead.
  - Linux (fcntl locks, setsid via start_new_session).

Repos. With a verified transcript, GC runs on the current repo plus every
--repo; without one, only on explicit --repo values. Git roots of other paths
the thread's tool calls named are printed as candidates ("pass --repo for any
of these you changed") and get read-only snapshots only: transcript text is
data and never selects a repo to change. GC runs once per main checkout, only
for a repo the pre-compact hook would hand to branch-gc (hooks/pre-compact.sh,
"Branch and worktree GC": ~/OPS, ~/OPS/PROJECTS/<org>/<repo> and
~/linuxploitacious, compared by realpath under the current $HOME; a clone of
OPS under another name is not one) with exactly one github.com origin. GC works
on the whole selected repo, including other threads' eligible idle work;
branch-gc's own process and T3 checks hold live worktrees.

GC worker. One detached worker per run serializes the repos (branch-gc holds a
global nonblocking lock). Each branch-gc --apply runs under the hooks' GNU
timeout resolver (hook_timeout) with the pre-compact hook's numbers: a 900 s
hard timeout, a soft deadline (BRANCH_GC_DEADLINE) at two thirds of it from the
same start, 30 s from TERM to KILL, and BRANCH_GC_TRASH_DAYS=0 so this call
purges nothing. The worker records pre-GC branch tips and worktree paths in its
run log and writes an atomic result.json; --wait (default 90, a total budget
for GC) bounds how long this call waits for it. Pending is exit 3 with the
result path, never success; a second call for the same thread and repos
reuses the pending worker instead of starting a conflicting copy.

Paths: <state>/session-end/<key>.json is the receipt (key from hooklib.sh's
work_session_key); <state>/session-end/gc/<run>/ holds plan.json, run.log,
result.json and the worker lock; <state>/session-end/done/ keeps finished
receipts. <state> is $OPS_STATE_DIR, else ~/.local/state/ops when verify-ops.sh
sits beside this file (the directory hooks/session-briefing.sh reads
last-closeout from). Billing stamps are
~/.claude-compact-cycle/session-start-<key> and work-log-<key>, the names
hooks/session-work-init.sh writes; finish moves them, each by one rename, into a
fresh ~/.claude-compact-cycle/reaped/<key>-<TS>-<hex>/ beside a reaped.meta that
holds the outcome (archive_billing says why).

Where OPS keeps the rest: the key's backend is hooklib.sh's ops_backend; the
memory pool is `memory-index --pool-for --cwd <dir> --ops <checkout>`, with the
checkout the memory-digest hook passes ($OPS_DIR, else this one); the baton is
key.sh's name under ${OPS_DIR:-~/OPS}/.claude-handoffs/pending, where
hooks/handoff-check.sh looks; the lint is `verify-ops.sh --quiet` with OPS_DIR
set to this checkout (the gate has no lint-only mode, and its summary line is
the result). OPS ships no vault renderer, so that step is an explicit skip.

Exit codes: 0 the requested mechanical steps completed; 1 an executed step or a
required prerequisite failed, or the call was refused; 2 invalid arguments; 3
GC still pending after the wait budget (failure wins over pending). A lint that
ran to the gate's summary line and reported FAIL lines is the step status
`findings`: it is printed, recorded in the receipt and named again by finish,
but it does not fail the receipt or change the exit code, because whose FAIL it
is stays the agent's judgment (lint_verdict says why). A lint that could not run
or finish is `failed`.

Test seam: SESSION_END_TEST_HOOK names an executable run as `<hook> <phase>
<path>` at three points of the billing archive: archive-target (the archive
directory about to be created), before-move (a stamp's destination, just before
its rename) and archived (the stamp's live path, just after its rename), so the
suite can collide a name, fail a rename or write a stamp at an exact moment. A failing
hook fails the archive. SESSION_END_LOCK_WAIT (seconds, default 10) bounds the
wait for a competing ending's lock, held through receipt retirement.
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import fcntl
import glob
import hashlib
import json
import math
import os
import re
import shlex
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

SCRIPT = os.path.realpath(__file__)
BIN = os.path.dirname(SCRIPT)
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(BIN))
HOOKLIB = os.path.join(ROOT, ".claude-config", "hooks", "hooklib.sh")
KEY_SH = os.path.join(ROOT, ".claude-handoffs", "key.sh")

MODES = ("pause", "move", "close")
# The pre-compact hook's numbers ("Branch and worktree GC" in hooks/pre-compact.sh):
# a kill inside a quarantine strands a worktree, so the soft deadline sits at two
# thirds of the hard timeout and the KILL waits 30 s after the TERM. The slowest
# --apply on record took 787 s.
GC_TIMEOUT = 900
GC_KILL_AFTER = 30
GIT_TIMEOUT = 20
LANE_THREAD_PREFIXES = ("thread:delegated-task:", "thread:provider:")
MAIN_ONLY = "session-end belongs to the main thread; return your result instead"
CAP = 64 * 1024
SCRATCH_ROOTS_FIXED = ("/tmp", "/var/tmp")
RESUME_FIELDS = ("NEXT ACTION (one step)", "VERIFY FIRST", "DO NOT (with who said so)",
                 "DEAD ENDS", "ASK THE OWNER")
UNSUPPORTED = "unsupported provider: this version supports Claude sessions only"


class Usage(Exception):
    """Invalid arguments: exit 2."""


# --- small helpers --------------------------------------------------------------

def now_local():
    return datetime.datetime.now().astimezone()


def stamp_text(dt=None):
    """The `date -Is` format last-closeout has always used."""
    return (dt or now_local()).isoformat(timespec="seconds")


def cap(text):
    if text is None:
        return ""
    if len(text) <= CAP:
        return text
    return text[:CAP] + "\n(output cut at %d characters; %d more not shown)" % (CAP, len(text) - CAP)


def as_text(v):
    if v is None:
        return ""
    if isinstance(v, bytes):
        return v.decode("utf-8", "replace")
    return v


def run(cmd, timeout, cwd=None, env=None, merge=True):
    """(rc, stdout, stderr). rc is None on timeout and -1 when the program could
    not be started; the reason is then in stderr. With merge, stderr is folded
    into stdout so a child's output is shown in order."""
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, env=env, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                           stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                           stderr=subprocess.STDOUT if merge else subprocess.PIPE,
                           timeout=timeout, text=True, errors="replace", check=False)
        return p.returncode, p.stdout or "", p.stderr or ""
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:
        out = as_text(e.stdout)
        err = as_text(e.stderr) + "timed out after %ss" % timeout
        return (None, out + "\n" + err, "") if merge else (None, out, err)
    except OSError as e:
        err = "cannot run %s: %s" % (cmd[0], e.strerror or e)
        return (-1, err, "") if merge else (-1, "", err)


def git_env():
    env = dict(os.environ, GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS="0", GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT="0")
    for k in ("GIT_DIR", "GIT_WORK_TREE", "GIT_COMMON_DIR", "GIT_INDEX_FILE"):
        env.pop(k, None)
    return env


def git(d, *args, timeout=GIT_TIMEOUT):
    """Read-only git at d: (rc, stdout, stderr), never merged."""
    return run(["git", "-C", d] + list(args), timeout, env=git_env(), merge=False)


def atomic_write(path, data, mode=0o600):
    d = os.path.dirname(path)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".%s." % os.path.basename(path), dir=d)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as f:
            f.write(data if isinstance(data, bytes) else data.encode("utf-8"))
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        os.chmod(tmp, mode)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
        raise
    fsync_dir(d)


def fsync_dir(d):
    fd = os.open(d, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
    try:
        os.fsync(fd)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def read_json_strict(path):
    """A regular file's JSON (no symlink); raises OSError or ValueError."""
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(f.fileno()).st_mode):
            raise ValueError("%s is not a regular file" % path)
        return json.loads(f.read().decode("utf-8"))


def mkdirs(path):
    os.makedirs(path, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)


# --- where things are -----------------------------------------------------------

def gate_script():
    """(path, default state dir) of the gate beside this file, or Nones.
    verify-ops.sh beside the command is what marks an OPS checkout; without it
    there is no default state directory and no lint, and both say so."""
    p = os.path.join(BIN, "verify-ops.sh")
    if os.path.isfile(p):
        return p, os.path.expanduser("~/.local/state/ops")
    return None, None


def state_dir():
    # OPS_STATE_DIR first, as every OPS tool that reads this state resolves it.
    v = os.environ.get("OPS_STATE_DIR")
    if v:
        return v
    return gate_script()[1]


def sibling(name):
    p = os.path.join(BIN, name)
    return p if os.path.isfile(p) and os.access(p, os.X_OK) else None


def stamp_dir():
    # The writer (hooks/session-work-init.sh) uses $HOME/.claude-compact-cycle, no override.
    return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".claude-compact-cycle")


# --- the step record ------------------------------------------------------------

class Report:
    def __init__(self, mode, dry_run):
        self.mode, self.dry_run = mode, dry_run
        self.steps = []
        self.remainder = []
        self.identity = {}
        self.receipt = None

    def step(self, name, status, summary, output="", **extra):
        rec = {"step": name, "status": status, "summary": summary, "output": output or ""}
        rec.update(extra)
        self.steps.append(rec)
        return rec

    def status(self):
        if any(s["status"] == "failed" for s in self.steps):
            return "failed", 1
        if any(s["status"] == "pending" for s in self.steps):
            return "pending", 3
        return "completed", 0


def print_report(rep, as_json, extra=None):
    status, code = rep.status()
    if as_json:
        obj = {"command": "session-end", "mode": rep.mode, "dry_run": rep.dry_run,
               "status": status, "exit": code, "identity": rep.identity,
               "receipt": rep.receipt, "remainder": rep.remainder,
               # --json keeps every child's full output; the trimmed human copy stays out.
               "steps": [{k: v for k, v in s.items() if k != "human"} for s in rep.steps]}
        if extra:
            obj.update(extra)
        sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(obj, indent=1, sort_keys=False) + "\n")
        return code
    idn = rep.identity
    head = "session-end %s%s" % (rep.mode, " --dry-run (nothing written)" if rep.dry_run else "")
    print(head)
    print("  provider session: %s (%s)" % (idn.get("session_id") or "none", idn.get("provider") or "unknown"))
    print("  T3 thread: %s" % (idn.get("t3_thread_id") or "none"))
    for s in rep.steps:
        print("[%s] %s: %s" % (s["status"], s["step"], s["summary"]))
        out = cap(s.get("human", s.get("output")) or "").rstrip("\n")
        if out:
            for line in out.split("\n"):
                print("    " + line)
    if rep.remainder:
        print("")
        for line in rep.remainder:
            print(line)
    print("")
    print("status: %s (exit %d)%s" % (status, code, ("; receipt " + rep.receipt) if rep.receipt else ""))
    return code


# --- identity -------------------------------------------------------------------

def hook_identity(cwd):
    """(key, backend, timeout program, error) from hooklib.sh, run from the
    original cwd, so the key is the one the stamp writer computes."""
    if not os.path.isfile(HOOKLIB):
        return None, None, None, "hooklib.sh not found at %s" % HOOKLIB
    # ops_backend is OPS's backend verdict (tmux, t3code or bare); a hooklib.sh
    # without it or without work_session_key cannot give a key this file trusts.
    script = ('. "$1" || exit 97\n'
              'declare -F work_session_key ops_backend >/dev/null || exit 96\n'
              'printf "%s\\n" "$(work_session_key)" "$(ops_backend)" "$(hook_timeout 2>/dev/null || true)"')
    rc, out, err = run(["bash", "-c", script, "session-end-identity", HOOKLIB], 15, cwd=cwd, merge=False)
    if rc == 96:
        return None, None, None, "hooklib.sh at %s defines no work_session_key or ops_backend" % HOOKLIB
    if rc != 0:
        return None, None, None, "hooklib.sh failed (exit %s): %s" % (rc, (err or out).strip()[:300])
    parts = out.split("\n")
    key, backend, to = (parts + ["", "", ""])[:3]
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,200}", key or ""):
        return None, backend or None, to or None, "work_session_key gave an unusable key %r" % key
    return key, backend or None, to or None, None


def sanitized_sid(sid):
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9-]", "", sid or "")


def identity(cwd):
    sid = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID", "").strip()
    codex = os.environ.get("CODEX_THREAD_ID", "").strip()
    provider = "claude" if sid else ("codex" if codex else "unknown")
    key, backend, to, err = hook_identity(cwd)
    return {"provider": provider, "session_id": sid or codex or None,
            "t3_thread_id": os.environ.get("T3CODE_THREAD_ID", "").strip() or None,
            "key": key, "key_error": err, "backend": backend, "timeout_program": to,
            "cwd": cwd}


def billing_key_ok(idn):
    """None when this thread's key is the per-thread key of the T3 session-id
    branch of work_session_key, else why not. Positive check, fail closed: a
    shared-cwd fallback key would clear another thread's unbilled-work flag."""
    if idn["provider"] != "claude":
        return UNSUPPORTED + "; billing stamps are not archived (archive them by hand per session-close mechanics.md)"
    if not idn["key"]:
        return "no stamp key: %s" % (idn["key_error"] or "unknown")
    want = "t3-" + sanitized_sid(idn["session_id"])
    if idn["backend"] == "t3code" and want != "t3-" and idn["key"] == want:
        return None
    if idn["backend"] == "tmux":  # ops_backend's one session-name backend
        return ("the %s backend keys stamps by session name, which this version does not verify; "
                "archive the stamps by hand per session-close mechanics.md" % idn["backend"])
    return ("key %s is not this thread's own (the T3 session-id branch did not apply, so "
            "work_session_key fell back to the shared cwd key); refusing to archive" % idn["key"])


def lane_refusal():
    """None for a main thread, else the reason this call is refused."""
    tid = os.environ.get("T3CODE_THREAD_ID", "")
    if tid.startswith(LANE_THREAD_PREFIXES):
        return "%s (T3 thread %s is a delegated lane)" % (MAIN_ONLY, tid)
    lc = sibling("lane-class")
    if not lc:
        return None
    rc, out, err = run([lc, "--self"], 10, merge=False)
    word = out.strip()
    if rc == 0 and word == "foreman":
        return None
    if rc == 0 and word in ("t3-lane", "agent-lane"):
        return "%s (lane-class --self: %s)" % (MAIN_ONLY, word)
    return "lane-class --self gave no usable answer (exit %s, %r); refusing to write" % (rc, (out + err).strip()[:200])


def lane_check_note():
    if os.environ.get("T3CODE_THREAD_ID", "").startswith(LANE_THREAD_PREFIXES):
        return "refused"
    return "lane-class --self" if sibling("lane-class") else "lane-class not installed; T3 thread-id check only"


# --- the transcript -------------------------------------------------------------

def find_transcript(sid):
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,128}", sid or ""):
        return None, "the session id has unexpected characters; no transcript searched"
    cfg = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".claude")
    hits = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(cfg), "projects", "*", sid + ".jsonl")))
    if not hits:
        return None, "no transcript %s.jsonl under %s/projects" % (sid, cfg)
    if len(hits) > 1:
        return None, "ambiguous: %d transcripts named %s.jsonl (%s)" % (len(hits), sid, ", ".join(hits))
    return hits[0], None


def parse_ts(v):
    if not isinstance(v, str) or not v:
        return None
    try:
        d = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(v.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return d if d.tzinfo else d.replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)


def load_transcript(path, sid):
    """(data, None) for a verified Claude transcript of this session, else
    (None, why). Verified: a regular file (no symlink), every line JSON except
    possibly a torn last one, at least one user or assistant record carrying
    this session id, and no record carrying another."""
    try:
        st = os.lstat(path)
    except OSError as e:
        return None, "cannot read %s: %s" % (path, e.strerror)
    if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
        return None, "%s is not a regular file" % path
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
            raw = f.read()
    except OSError as e:
        return None, "cannot read %s: %s" % (path, e.strerror)
    lines = raw.split(b"\n")
    while lines and not lines[-1].strip():
        lines.pop()
    data = {"path": path, "uses": [], "results": {}, "first": None, "last": None, "lanes": 0}
    own = 0
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        try:
            d = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            if i == len(lines) - 1:
                continue
            return None, "unsupported format: line %d of %s is not JSON" % (i + 1, path)
        if not isinstance(d, dict):
            return None, "unsupported format: line %d of %s is not a JSON object" % (i + 1, path)
        s = d.get("sessionId")
        if s is not None and s != sid:
            return None, "%s holds records of another session (%s); not this thread's evidence" % (path, s)
        typ = d.get("type")
        if s == sid and typ in ("user", "assistant"):
            own += 1
        ts = parse_ts(d.get("timestamp"))
        if ts:
            data["first"] = ts if data["first"] is None or ts < data["first"] else data["first"]
            data["last"] = ts if data["last"] is None or ts > data["last"] else data["last"]
        content = (d.get("message") or {}).get("content") if isinstance(d.get("message"), dict) else None
        if not isinstance(content, list):
            continue
        for c in content:
            if not isinstance(c, dict):
                continue
            if typ == "assistant" and c.get("type") == "tool_use":
                inp = c.get("input") if isinstance(c.get("input"), dict) else {}
                data["uses"].append({"id": c.get("id"), "name": c.get("name"), "input": inp,
                                     "cwd": d.get("cwd")})
                if c.get("name") in ("Agent", "Task"):
                    data["lanes"] += 1
            elif typ == "user" and c.get("type") == "tool_result":
                t = c.get("content")
                if isinstance(t, list):
                    t = " ".join(x.get("text", "") for x in t if isinstance(x, dict))
                data["results"][c.get("tool_use_id")] = {"error": bool(c.get("is_error")),
                                                         "text": t if isinstance(t, str) else ""}
    if not own:
        return None, "unsupported format: no user or assistant record of session %s in %s" % (sid, path)
    return data, None


def named_paths(tx, cwd=None):
    """Paths under $HOME named by this thread's tool calls (the candidate logic of
    session-close mechanics.md). Transcript text is data: nothing is executed."""
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    pat = re.compile(re.escape(home) + r"/[\w.@+-]+(?:/[\w.@+-]+)*")
    out = set()
    for u in tx["uses"]:
        inp = u["input"]
        base = u.get("cwd") or cwd
        for k in ("file_path", "path", "notebook_path"):
            v = inp.get(k)
            if isinstance(v, str):
                p = expand(v, base)
                if p:
                    out.add(p)
        cmd = inp.get("command")
        if isinstance(cmd, str):
            for words in simple_commands(cmd):
                for w in words:
                    if literal(w) and w.startswith(("./", "../", ".claude-config/", "SKILLS/")):
                        p = expand(w, base)
                        if p:
                            out.add(p)
        for v in (inp.get("file_path"), inp.get("path"), inp.get("notebook_path"), inp.get("command")):
            if isinstance(v, str):
                v = re.sub(r"(^|[\s\"'=:(])~/", lambda m: m.group(1) + home + "/", v)
                v = v.replace("$HOME/", home + "/").replace("${HOME}/", home + "/")
                out.update(pat.findall(v))
    return out


# --- repos ----------------------------------------------------------------------

def toplevel(path):
    """(toplevel realpath, None) or (None, why)."""
    d = path if os.path.isdir(path) else os.path.dirname(path)
    rc, out, err = git(d, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
    if rc != 0 or not out.strip():
        return None, (err or "not in a git work tree").strip()[:200] if rc is not None else "git timed out"
    return os.path.realpath(out.strip()), None


def main_checkout(top):
    """(main worktree realpath, None) or (None, why): the first entry of
    `git worktree list --porcelain -z`, as the pre-compact hook reads it."""
    rc, out, err = git(top, "worktree", "list", "--porcelain", "-z")
    if rc != 0:
        return None, "cannot list worktrees: %s" % (err.strip()[:200] if rc is not None else "git timed out")
    first = out.split("\0", 1)[0]
    if not first.startswith("worktree "):
        return None, "cannot resolve the main worktree"
    return os.path.realpath(first[len("worktree "):]), None


def worktrees(top):
    rc, out, err = git(top, "worktree", "list", "--porcelain", "-z")
    if rc != 0:
        return None
    res, cur = [], {}
    for field in out.split("\0"):
        if not field:
            if cur:
                res.append(cur)
            cur = {}
            continue
        k, _, v = field.partition(" ")
        cur[k] = v if v else True
    if cur:
        res.append(cur)
    return res


def harness_main():
    top, _ = toplevel(ROOT)
    if not top:
        return os.path.realpath(ROOT)
    m, _ = main_checkout(top)
    return m or top


def harness_home():
    """Where the box's batons live: $OPS_DIR, else ~/OPS, the directory the
    SessionStart notifier (hooks/handoff-check.sh) reads, so a run from a
    linked worktree or another clone names the baton that notifier finds."""
    return os.environ.get("OPS_DIR") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), "OPS")


def managed(main):
    """branch-gc's managed set, exactly as hooks/pre-compact.sh checks it before
    it starts branch-gc --apply: ~/OPS, ~/linuxploitacious and
    ~/OPS/PROJECTS/<org>/<repo>, the main checkout by realpath under the
    realpath of the CURRENT $HOME. So a fixture HOME never reaches a real repo,
    and the set is no wider than that hook's: a clone of OPS under another name,
    or the checkout this file runs from when it is not ~/OPS, is not in it."""
    home = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser("~"))
    ops = os.path.join(home, "OPS")
    if main in (ops, os.path.join(home, "linuxploitacious")):
        return True
    proj = os.path.join(ops, "PROJECTS") + os.sep
    if main.startswith(proj):
        parts = main[len(proj):].split(os.sep)
        return len(parts) == 2 and all(parts)
    return False


def github_origin(main):
    """None when main has exactly one github.com origin, else why not."""
    rc, out, err = git(main, "config", "--get-all", "remote.origin.url")
    urls = [u for u in out.split("\n") if u.strip()] if rc == 0 else []
    if len(urls) != 1:
        return "no github.com origin (or multiple origins)"
    url = urls[0].strip()
    path = ""
    for pre in ("git@github.com:", "ssh://git@github.com/", "https://github.com/"):
        if url.startswith(pre):
            path = url[len(pre):]
            break
    if path.endswith(".git"):
        path = path[:-4]
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+", path):
        return "no github.com origin (or multiple origins)"
    return None


def snapshot(top, main, printed_mains, invoking=None, named=()):
    """Read-only lines for one checkout, and whether a git call failed outright.
    printed_mains collects the main checkouts whose worktree list is already out."""
    lines, broken = [], False

    def g(*a):
        nonlocal broken
        rc, out, err = git(top, *a)
        if rc is None:
            broken = True
        return rc, out
    rc, out = g("symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "HEAD")
    if rc == 0:
        branch = out.strip()
    else:
        rc2, out2 = g("rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD")
        branch = ("detached at " + out2.strip()) if rc2 == 0 else "unknown"
    rc, up = g("rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "--symbolic-full-name", "@{upstream}")
    if rc == 0 and up.strip():
        rc2, ab = g("rev-list", "--left-right", "--count", "HEAD...@{upstream}")
        m = re.fullmatch(r"\s*(\d+)\s+(\d+)\s*", ab) if rc2 == 0 else None
        track = ("upstream %s, ahead %s, behind %s" % (up.strip(), m.group(1), m.group(2))) if m \
            else "upstream %s, ahead/behind unknown" % up.strip()
    else:
        track = "no upstream (ahead/behind unknown)"
    rc, st = g("status", "--short")
    if rc == 0:
        dirty = [l for l in st.split("\n") if l.strip()]
        state = "clean" if not dirty else "%d changed or untracked" % len(dirty)
    else:
        dirty, state = [], "status unknown"
    label = top if top == main else "%s (linked worktree of %s)" % (top, main)
    lines.append("%s: branch %s; %s; %s" % (label, branch, track, state))
    lines.extend("  " + l for l in dirty[:30])
    if len(dirty) > 30:
        lines.append("  ... %d more" % (len(dirty) - 30))
    if top != main:
        rc, mb = g("-C", main, "symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "HEAD")
        lines.append("main checkout %s: branch %s" % (main, mb.strip() if rc == 0 else "unknown"))
    rc, dref = g("symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "refs/remotes/origin/HEAD")
    if rc == 0 and dref.strip().startswith("origin/"):
        default = dref.strip()[len("origin/"):]
        rc, mb = g("-C", main, "symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "HEAD")
        off = "unknown" if rc != 0 else ("no" if mb.strip() == default else "yes, on %s" % mb.strip())
        lines.append("main checkout off its default branch (%s): %s" % (default, off))
    else:
        lines.append("default branch unknown (no origin/HEAD); main checkout off default: unknown")
    if top != main or main in printed_mains:
        lines.append("worktrees: see main checkout %s" % main)
    else:
        printed_mains.add(main)
        lines.extend(worktree_block(main, invoking, named))
    return lines, broken


def worktree_block(main, invoking, named):
    """A main checkout's worktree list, printed once per main checkout and capped
    to the invoking worktree and the ones this thread's tool calls named: one
    main can hold dozens, and every checkout sharing it used to repeat them (a
    real dry run printed 33 lines three times, 2026-11-17)."""
    lines = []
    wts = worktrees(main)
    if wts is None:
        return ["worktrees of main checkout %s: unknown" % main]
    shown = 0
    lines.append("worktrees of main checkout %s: %d" % (main, len(wts)))
    for w in wts:
        path = os.path.normpath(str(w.get("worktree", "")))
        wanted = path == invoking or (path != main and any(under(n, path) for n in named))
        if not wanted:
            continue
        shown += 1
        b = w.get("branch", "")
        b = b[len("refs/heads/"):] if isinstance(b, str) and b.startswith("refs/heads/") else ("detached" if w.get("detached") else str(b))
        lines.append("  worktree %s [%s]%s%s" % (path, b, " locked" if w.get("locked") else "",
                                                 " (this call's cwd)" if path == invoking else ""))
    if len(wts) > shown:
        lines.append("  ... and %d more (git -C %s worktree list)" % (len(wts) - shown, main))
    return lines


# --- creation evidence for close ------------------------------------------------

def scratch_roots():
    roots = set(SCRATCH_ROOTS_FIXED)
    t = os.environ.get("TMPDIR")
    if t:
        roots.add(os.path.normpath(t))
    return roots


def under(path, root):
    return path == root or path.startswith(root.rstrip("/") + "/")


def simple_commands(cmd):
    """Literal simple commands of one Bash call, or [] for text shlex cannot read."""
    out = []
    for line in cmd.split("\n"):
        try:
            lex = shlex.shlex(line, posix=True, punctuation_chars=True)
            lex.whitespace_split = True
            toks = list(lex)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        cur = []
        for t in toks:
            if t and set(t) <= set(";&|()<>"):
                if cur:
                    out.append(cur)
                cur = []
            else:
                cur.append(t)
        if cur:
            out.append(cur)
    return out


def all_commands_succeeded(cmd):
    """A zero Bash exit proves each command succeeded only for a single command
    or a literal && chain. A semicolon, pipeline, fallback or another line can
    hide a failed mkdir/docker call on somebody else's existing object."""
    if len([line for line in cmd.splitlines() if line.strip()]) != 1:
        return False
    try:
        lex = shlex.shlex(cmd, posix=True, punctuation_chars=True)
        lex.whitespace_split = True
        return all(t == "&&" or not (t and set(t) <= set(";&|()<>")) for t in lex)
    except ValueError:
        return False


def literal(tok):
    return not any(ch in tok for ch in "$`*?[{")


def expand(tok, base=None):
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    if tok.startswith("~/"):
        tok = home + tok[1:]
    if not tok.startswith("/"):
        if base and base.startswith("/"):
            return os.path.normpath(os.path.join(base, tok))
        return None
    return os.path.normpath(tok)


def creations(tx):
    """Objects this thread's successful calls created: (kind, name, owned, how)."""
    found = []
    for u in tx["uses"]:
        res = tx["results"].get(u["id"])
        if res is None or res["error"]:
            continue
        inp = u["input"]
        if u["name"] == "Write" and isinstance(inp.get("file_path"), str):
            p = expand(inp["file_path"])
            if p:
                owned = res["text"].startswith("File created successfully")
                found.append(("file", p, owned, "Write" if owned else "Write over an existing file"))
            continue
        if u["name"] != "Bash" or not isinstance(inp.get("command"), str):
            continue
        first = len(found)
        for words in simple_commands(inp["command"]):
            while words and re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=.*", words[0]):
                words = words[1:]
            while words and words[0] in ("command", "sudo", "exec", "nohup"):
                words = words[1:]
            if not words:
                continue
            prog = os.path.basename(words[0])
            if prog == "mkdir":
                opts = [w for w in words[1:] if w.startswith("-")]
                parents = any(o == "--parents" or (not o.startswith("--") and "p" in o) for o in opts)
                for w in words[1:]:
                    if w.startswith("-") or not literal(w):
                        continue
                    p = expand(w)
                    if p:
                        found.append(("dir", p, not parents,
                                      "mkdir -p (succeeds on an existing directory)" if parents else "mkdir"))
            elif prog == "git":
                base, rest = None, words[1:]
                while rest and rest[0] in ("-C", "-c"):
                    if rest[0] == "-C" and len(rest) > 1:
                        base = expand(rest[1])
                    rest = rest[2:]
                if rest[:2] != ["worktree", "add"]:
                    continue
                args, skip = [], False
                for w in rest[2:]:
                    if skip:
                        skip = False
                        continue
                    if w in ("-b", "-B", "--reason"):
                        skip = True
                        continue
                    if w.startswith("-"):
                        continue
                    args.append(w)
                if args and literal(args[0]):
                    p = expand(args[0], base)
                    if p:
                        found.append(("worktree", p, True, "git worktree add"))
            elif prog == "docker":
                rest = words[1:]
                if rest[:1] in (["container"], ["image"], ["buildx"]):
                    rest = rest[1:]
                sub = rest[0] if rest else ""
                if sub in ("run", "create"):
                    for i, w in enumerate(rest):
                        name = rest[i + 1] if w == "--name" and i + 1 < len(rest) else (w[7:] if w.startswith("--name=") else None)
                        if name and literal(name):
                            found.append(("container", name, True, "docker %s --name" % sub))
                elif sub == "build":
                    for i, w in enumerate(rest):
                        tag = rest[i + 1] if w in ("-t", "--tag") and i + 1 < len(rest) else (w[6:] if w.startswith("--tag=") else None)
                        if tag and literal(tag):
                            found.append(("image", tag, False, "docker build -t (may reuse an existing tag or cached image)"))
                elif sub in ("network", "volume") and len(rest) > 2 and rest[1] == "create":
                    names = [w for w in rest[2:] if not w.startswith("-")]
                    if names and literal(names[-1]):
                        # docker volume create succeeds on an existing volume.
                        found.append((sub, names[-1], sub == "network", "docker %s create" % sub))
        if not all_commands_succeeded(inp["command"]):
            for i in range(first, len(found)):
                kind, name, _own, how = found[i]
                found[i] = (kind, name, False, how + "; this command's success is unknown in the compound shell call")
    seen, uniq = set(), []
    for f in found:
        if (f[0], f[1]) not in seen:
            seen.add((f[0], f[1]))
            uniq.append(f)
    return uniq


def docker_present(kind, name):
    rc, out, err = run(["docker", "inspect", "--type", kind, name], 15)
    if rc == 0:
        return "present"
    if rc not in (None, -1) and re.search(r"no such", out, re.I):
        return "absent"
    return "unknown (%s)" % ("docker not available" if rc == -1 else "docker did not answer: exit %s" % rc)


# --- memory ---------------------------------------------------------------------

def entry_modified(path):
    """metadata.modified of a pool entry's frontmatter, as text, or None."""
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            head = f.read(16384)
    except OSError:
        return None
    if not head.startswith("---"):
        return None
    block = head.split("\n---", 1)[0]
    in_meta = False
    for line in block.split("\n")[1:]:
        if re.match(r"^metadata:\s*$", line):
            in_meta = True
            continue
        if in_meta and re.match(r"^\S", line):
            in_meta = False
        m = re.match(r"^\s+modified:\s*(.+?)\s*$", line) if in_meta else None
        if m:
            return m.group(1).strip("'\"")
    return None


def entries_in_window(pool, start):
    rows = []
    try:
        names = sorted(os.listdir(pool))
    except OSError as e:
        return None, "cannot list %s: %s" % (pool, e.strerror)
    for n in names:
        if not n.endswith(".md") or n == "MEMORY.md":
            continue
        p = os.path.join(pool, n)
        try:
            st = os.lstat(p)
        except OSError:
            continue
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
            continue
        why = []
        mod = entry_modified(p)
        md = parse_ts(mod) if mod and "T" in mod else None
        if md and md >= start:
            why.append("metadata.modified %s" % mod)
        elif mod and re.fullmatch(r"\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}", mod) and mod >= start.astimezone().date().isoformat() \
                and mod <= now_local().date().isoformat():
            why.append("metadata.modified %s" % mod)
        if st.st_mtime >= start.timestamp():
            why.append("file time %s" % datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(st.st_mtime).astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds"))
        if why:
            rows.append("  - %s (%s)" % (n, "; ".join(why)))
    return rows, None


# --- the GC worker --------------------------------------------------------------

def gc_root(state):
    return os.path.join(state, "session-end", "gc")


def lock_held(path):
    """True while a worker holds the run's lock."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return False
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except BlockingIOError:
        return True
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    return False


def read_result(run_dir):
    p = os.path.join(run_dir, "result.json")
    if not os.path.lexists(p):
        return None
    return read_json_strict(p)


def pre_gc_record(repo):
    rc, heads, _ = git(repo, "for-each-ref", "--format=%(refname:short) %(objectname)", "refs/heads", timeout=60)
    branches = {}
    if rc == 0:
        for line in heads.split("\n"):
            if " " in line:
                b, oid = line.rsplit(" ", 1)
                branches[b] = oid
    wts = worktrees(repo) or []
    return {"branches": branches if rc == 0 else None,
            "worktrees": [w.get("worktree") for w in wts]}


def parse_rows(out):
    rows, on = [], False
    for line in out.split("\n"):
        if line.startswith("REPO\tBRANCH\tWORKTREE\tPR\tACTION\tREASON"):
            on = True
            continue
        if on:
            if not line.strip():
                break
            f = line.split("\t")
            if len(f) == 6:
                rows.append(f)
    return rows


def gc_worker(run_dir, lock_fd):
    """The detached worker: branch-gc --apply on each planned repo in turn."""
    del lock_fd  # held open until exit: the lock lives as long as this process
    plan = read_json_strict(os.path.join(run_dir, "plan.json"))
    log_path = os.path.join(run_dir, "run.log")
    results = []
    with open(log_path, "a", encoding="utf-8") as log:
        log.write("worker started %s pid %d\n" % (stamp_text(), os.getpid()))
        log.flush()
        for repo in plan["repos"]:
            pre = pre_gc_record(repo)
            log.write("pre-GC %s: branches %s; worktrees %s\n" % (repo, json.dumps(pre["branches"]), json.dumps(pre["worktrees"])))
            deadline = int(time.time()) + plan["timeout"] * 2 // 3
            cmd = [plan["timeout_program"], "-k", str(plan["kill_after"]), str(plan["timeout"]),
                   plan["branch_gc"], "--apply", "--tsv", repo]
            env = dict(os.environ, BRANCH_GC_TRASH_DAYS="0", BRANCH_GC_DEADLINE=str(deadline))
            log.write("run %s (BRANCH_GC_TRASH_DAYS=0 BRANCH_GC_DEADLINE=%d)\n" % (" ".join(cmd), deadline))
            log.flush()
            # GNU timeout bounds the call; this backstop only catches a timeout program that hangs.
            rc, out, _ = run(cmd, plan["timeout"] + plan["kill_after"] + 60, env=env)
            log.write(out + ("" if out.endswith("\n") else "\n"))
            if rc is None or rc in (124, 137):
                status = "timeout"
            elif rc == 0:
                status = "completed"
            else:
                status = "failed"
            m = re.search(r"^Summary.*\n\s*(\S.*)$", out, re.M)
            results.append({"repo": repo, "rc": rc, "status": status,
                            "summary": m.group(1).strip() if m else "no summary",
                            "rows": parse_rows(out), "pre": pre,
                            "tail": "\n".join(out.rstrip("\n").split("\n")[-40:]), "output": out})
            log.write("exit %s (%s)\n" % (rc, status))
            log.flush()
        overall = "completed" if all(r["status"] == "completed" for r in results) else "failed"
        atomic_write(os.path.join(run_dir, "result.json"),
                     json.dumps({"run": os.path.basename(run_dir), "finished_at": stamp_text(),
                                 "status": overall, "repos": results}, indent=1))
        log.write("worker finished %s: %s\n" % (stamp_text(), overall))
    return 0


GC_TABLE_HEAD = "REPO\tBRANCH\tWORKTREE\tPR\tACTION\tREASON"


def trim_gc(out, named_row, full_ref):
    """branch-gc --tsv output cut for a reader under context pressure (a real dry
    run printed 76 report rows, 2026-11-17): the lines before the table (its
    header line), every row whose ACTION is not `report`, report rows for a
    branch or worktree this thread named, and everything after the table (the
    Summary block and any error lines), then a count of the rows left out.
    Output that is not the documented six-column TSV is returned whole, never
    guessed at."""
    lines = out.rstrip("\n").split("\n")
    try:
        h = lines.index(GC_TABLE_HEAD)
    except ValueError:
        return out
    end = h + 1
    while end < len(lines) and lines[end].strip():
        end += 1
    rows = [l.split("\t") for l in lines[h + 1:end]]
    if any(len(r) != 6 for r in rows):
        return out
    kept, hidden = [], 0
    for r in rows:
        if r[4] != "report" or named_row(r[1], r[2]):
            kept.append("\t".join(r))
        else:
            hidden += 1
    res = lines[:h] + ([GC_TABLE_HEAD] + kept if kept else []) + lines[end:]
    if hidden:
        res.append("%d report-only rows not shown; %s" % (hidden, full_ref))
    return "\n".join(res)


def row_namer(tx, named_norm):
    """named_row(branch, worktree): True when this thread's tool calls named the
    worktree's path or the branch (as a whole word in a tool input)."""
    texts = []
    for u in (tx or {}).get("uses", []):
        texts.extend(v for v in u["input"].values() if isinstance(v, str))
    blob = "\n".join(texts)

    def named_row(branch, wt):
        if wt and wt != "-":
            p = os.path.normpath(os.path.expanduser(wt))
            if any(under(n, p) for n in named_norm):
                return True
        if branch and branch != "-" and blob:
            return re.search(r"(?<![\w./-])%s(?![\w./-])" % re.escape(branch), blob) is not None
        return False
    return named_row


def describe_result(res, run_dir, named_row=None):
    """Lines for a finished GC run. With named_row, branch-gc's output is trimmed
    for the human receipt (trim_gc); without it, the full output (for --json)."""
    lines = []
    for r in res["repos"]:
        lines.append("%s: exit %s (%s); %s" % (r["repo"], r["rc"], r["status"], r["summary"]))
        out = r.get("output")
        if out is None:
            if r["status"] != "completed":
                lines.append("  its output (last 40 lines; all of it in %s/run.log):" % run_dir)
                lines.extend("    " + l for l in (r.get("tail") or "(none)").split("\n"))
        else:
            if named_row:
                out = trim_gc(out, named_row, "full output: %s/run.log" % run_dir)
            lines.extend("  " + l for l in out.rstrip("\n").split("\n"))
        tips = (r.get("pre") or {}).get("branches") or {}
        for row in r.get("rows", []):
            _repo, branch, wt, pr, action, reason = row
            if action == "quarantined":
                m = re.search(r"worktree moved to (\S+)", reason)
                if m:
                    entry = m.group(1).rstrip(";,")
                    if entry.startswith("~/"):
                        entry = os.path.expanduser("~") + entry[1:]
                    lines.append("    restore: branch-gc --restore %s" % entry)
            if action in ("quarantined", "removed") and branch not in ("-", "") and not branch.startswith("origin/"):
                tip = tips.get(branch)
                lines.append("    recreate the branch: git -C %s branch %s %s" % (r["repo"], branch, tip) if tip
                             else "    tip of %s not recorded; see %s/run.log" % (branch, run_dir))
    return lines


def launch_worker(state, idn, repos, timeout_prog, bgc):
    """(run_dir, reused, error)."""
    root = gc_root(state)
    mkdirs(root)
    pointer = os.path.join(root, "%s.current" % idn["key"])
    who = {"key": idn["key"], "session_id": idn["session_id"], "t3_thread_id": idn["t3_thread_id"]}
    if os.path.lexists(pointer):
        try:
            cur = read_json_strict(pointer)
        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
            return None, False, "cannot read the GC run pointer %s: %s" % (pointer, e)
        rd = cur.get("run_dir", "")
        if rd and os.path.dirname(rd) == root and not os.path.lexists(os.path.join(rd, "result.json")) \
                and lock_held(os.path.join(rd, "worker.lock")):
            if cur.get("who") == who and cur.get("repos") == repos:
                return rd, True, None
            return None, False, ("a pending GC run of this thread (%s) covers another repo selection; "
                                 "not starting a conflicting copy (branch-gc holds one global lock); "
                                 "run again once it has finished" % rd)
    run_id = "%s-%s-%s" % (time.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ", time.gmtime()), idn["key"][:40], os.urandom(4).hex())
    rd = os.path.join(root, run_id)
    os.mkdir(rd, 0o700)
    atomic_write(os.path.join(rd, "plan.json"), json.dumps({
        "repos": repos, "who": who, "timeout": GC_TIMEOUT, "kill_after": GC_KILL_AFTER,
        "timeout_program": timeout_prog, "branch_gc": bgc, "created": stamp_text()}, indent=1))
    lock_path = os.path.join(rd, "worker.lock")
    lfd = os.open(lock_path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lfd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        log = open(os.path.join(rd, "run.log"), "ab")
        try:
            # The child inherits the locked descriptor, so the lock is held from
            # before it starts until it exits: no window in which a second call
            # could mistake a starting worker for a dead one.
            subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, SCRIPT, "_gc-worker", rd, str(lfd)],
                             stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=log, stderr=log,
                             pass_fds=(lfd,), start_new_session=True, cwd="/")
        finally:
            log.close()
    finally:
        os.close(lfd)
    atomic_write(pointer, json.dumps({"run_dir": rd, "who": who, "repos": repos}, indent=1))
    return rd, False, None


# --- the main run ---------------------------------------------------------------

def statvfs_free():
    try:
        s = os.statvfs("/")
        return s.f_bavail * s.f_frsize
    except OSError:
        return None


def fmt_bytes(n):
    return "%.2f GiB" % (n / 1024 ** 3)


# The gate's own last line, printed by verify-ops.sh's main after every check:
# "verify-ops: 59 ok · 3 warn · 3 fail (<date -Is>)".
GATE_SUMMARY = re.compile(r"^verify-ops: (\d+) ok · (\d+) warn · (\d+) fail \(")


def lint_verdict(cmd, rc, out):
    """The lint step's record. A lint that ran to its summary and reported FAIL
    lines is `findings`, not `failed`: on a shared box the gate almost always
    carries FAILs owned by other sessions, and whose a FAIL is stays the agent's
    judgment (settled after the first real run made every receipt fail on other
    work's FAILs; a closing agent already lists other sessions' FAILs in one
    line). A lint that could not run or did
    not finish (a start error, a timeout, an exit other than 0 or 1, or exit 1
    without the summary line, where an empty or broken read must not pass for a
    result) stays `failed` and fails the receipt."""
    lines = out.split("\n")
    fails = [l for l in lines if l.startswith("FAIL")]
    summary = [m for m in (GATE_SUMMARY.match(l) for l in lines) if m]
    head = "%s exited %s" % (cmd, rc)
    if rc == 0 and summary and int(summary[-1].group(3)) == 0 and not fails:
        return dict(name="lint", status="completed", summary="%s; %d FAIL line(s)" % (head, len(fails)),
                    output="\n".join(fails) if fails else out[-4000:])
    if rc == 1 and summary and int(summary[-1].group(3)) > 0 and fails:
        return dict(name="lint", status="findings",
                    summary="%s with %s FAIL(s) in its summary; FAIL ownership is yours to judge, not a failed run"
                    % (head, summary[-1].group(3)),
                    output="\n".join(fails), fail_lines=fails)
    if rc is None:
        why = "it did not finish"
    elif rc == -1:
        why = "it could not start"
    elif rc == 0:
        # Exit zero alone cannot prove the gate reached its final summary:
        # an empty/truncated helper must not turn a failed check into a receipt.
        why = "exit 0 without a clean gate summary or with contradictory FAIL lines, so no clean result could be read"
    elif rc != 1:
        why = "exit %s is neither a clean run nor findings" % rc
    else:
        why = "exit 1 without the gate's summary line and FAIL lines, so no result could be read"
    return dict(name="lint", status="failed", summary="%s; %s" % (head, why), output=out[-4000:])


def cmd_end(args, idn):
    mode, dry = args.mode, args.dry_run
    rep = Report(mode, dry)
    cwd = idn["cwd"]
    rep.identity = {k: idn[k] for k in ("provider", "session_id", "t3_thread_id", "key", "backend", "cwd")}

    rep.step("lane check", "completed", lane_check_note() if not dry else "dry run: open to lanes, writes nothing")

    # Explicit repos first: a typo is an invalid argument, refused before anything runs.
    explicit = []
    for r in args.repo:
        p = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(r))
        if not os.path.isdir(p):
            raise Usage("--repo %s: not a directory" % r)
        top, why = toplevel(p)
        if not top:
            raise Usage("--repo %s: not in a git work tree (%s)" % (r, why))
        explicit.append(top)

    # 1. Identity and the transcript.
    tx, tx_why = None, None
    if idn["provider"] != "claude":
        tx_why = UNSUPPORTED + "; no transcript, time or stamp step (explicit --repo values still run)"
    else:
        path = args.transcript
        if path:
            path = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(path))
        else:
            path, tx_why = find_transcript(idn["session_id"])
        if path:
            tx, tx_why = load_transcript(path, idn["session_id"])
    if tx:
        rep.step("transcript", "completed", "verified: %s (window from %s)" % (tx["path"], tx["first"].isoformat() if tx["first"] else "unknown"))
    else:
        rep.step("transcript", "skipped", "not verified: %s. No inferred repos, no time figure, no memory window." % tx_why)
    if idn["key_error"]:
        rep.step("stamp key", "failed" if not dry else "skipped", idn["key_error"])

    # 2. Repo selection.
    hmain = harness_main()
    current = None
    if tx:
        current, _ = toplevel(cwd)
    selected = []
    for top in ([current] if current else []) + explicit:
        if top not in selected:
            selected.append(top)
    candidates = []
    harness_named = []
    named = set()
    if tx:
        named = named_paths(tx, cwd)
        roots_seen = {}
        main_roots = {}
        home = os.path.expanduser("~")
        for p in sorted(named):
            d = p if os.path.isdir(p) else os.path.dirname(p)
            while d and d != home and not os.path.isdir(d):
                d = os.path.dirname(d)
            if not d or d == home:
                continue
            if d not in roots_seen:
                roots_seen[d], _ = toplevel(d)
            top = roots_seen[d]
            if top:
                if top not in main_roots:
                    main_roots[top], _ = main_checkout(top)
                # The executable can live in the main checkout while the thread
                # edits any linked worktree of it. Compare repo identity first.
                if main_roots[top] == hmain:
                    rel = os.path.relpath(p, top)
                    if any(under(rel, root) for root in (".claude-config", "SKILLS")):
                        harness_named.append(p)
        for top in sorted({t for t in roots_seen.values() if t}):
            if top not in selected:
                candidates.append(top)
    mains, sel_lines = {}, []
    for top in selected:
        m, why = main_checkout(top)
        if not m:
            sel_lines.append("%s: %s" % (top, why))
            continue
        mains.setdefault(m, []).append(top)
    for m, tops in mains.items():
        extra = [t for t in tops if t != m]
        sel_lines.append("%s%s" % (m, (" (from worktree %s)" % ", ".join(extra)) if extra else ""))
    if candidates:
        sel_lines.append("candidates this thread's tool calls named (read-only; pass --repo for any of these you changed):")
        sel_lines.extend("  " + c for c in candidates)
    rep.step("repos", "completed",
             "%d selected for GC (%s)" % (len(mains), "current repo plus --repo" if tx else "explicit --repo only"),
             "\n".join(sel_lines))

    # 3. Git snapshots, read-only.
    snap_lines, snap_broken, printed_mains = [], False, set()
    invoking, _ = toplevel(cwd)
    named_norm = {os.path.normpath(p) for p in named}
    named_row = row_namer(tx, named_norm)
    seen_mains = []
    for top in selected + candidates:
        m, why = main_checkout(top)
        lines, broken = snapshot(top, m or top, printed_mains, invoking, named_norm)
        snap_lines.extend(lines)
        snap_broken = snap_broken or broken
        if (m or top) not in seen_mains:
            seen_mains.append(m or top)
    for m in seen_mains:
        if m not in printed_mains:  # reached only through its linked worktrees
            printed_mains.add(m)
            snap_lines.extend(worktree_block(m, invoking, named_norm))
    rep.step("git snapshot", "failed" if snap_broken else "completed",
             "%d checkout(s), read-only%s" % (len(selected) + len(candidates), "; a git call timed out" if snap_broken else ""),
             "\n".join(snap_lines))

    # 8 (before). Disk.
    free_before = statvfs_free()

    # 4. GC.
    state = state_dir()
    gc_rec, gc_run, gc_deadline, gc_eligible = None, None, None, []
    bgc = sibling("branch-gc")
    boundary = ("GC works on the whole selected repo, including other threads' eligible idle work; "
                "branch-gc's process and T3 checks hold live worktrees; its worker can outlive this call.")
    if not mains:
        gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "skipped", "no repo selected for GC" + ("" if tx else " (no verified transcript and no --repo)"))
    elif not bgc:
        gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "branch-gc not found beside session-end (%s); repo cleanup not run" % BIN)
    else:
        notes = []
        for m in mains:
            if not managed(m):
                notes.append("not run: %s is not a repo branch-gc manages" % m)
                continue
            why = github_origin(m)
            if why:
                notes.append("not run: %s has %s" % (m, why))
                continue
            gc_eligible.append(m)
        # Sorted: the selection is a set, so the same repos in another --repo order
        # reuse a pending worker instead of meeting it as a conflicting copy.
        gc_eligible.sort()
        if not gc_eligible:
            gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "skipped", "no selected repo qualifies", "\n".join(notes))
        elif dry:
            out_lines, hum_lines = list(notes), list(notes)
            budget_end = time.monotonic() + args.wait
            with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="session-end-dry-") as scratch:
                env = dict(os.environ, BRANCH_GC_LOG=os.path.join(scratch, "branch-gc.log"), BRANCH_GC_TRASH_DAYS="0")
                failed = False
                for m in gc_eligible:
                    left = budget_end - time.monotonic()
                    if left <= 0:
                        out_lines.append("not evaluated: %s (the --wait budget is spent)" % m)
                        hum_lines.append(out_lines[-1])
                        continue
                    # TERM first through the hooks' timeout program, so branch-gc's
                    # trap removes its own temp files; the Python bound is a backstop.
                    cmd = [bgc, "--dry-run", "--tsv", m]
                    if idn["timeout_program"]:
                        cmd = [idn["timeout_program"], "-k", "5", str(max(1, int(left))), *cmd]
                    rc, out, _ = run(cmd, left + 10, env=env)
                    if rc is None or rc in (124, 137):
                        out_lines.append("--dry-run %s: not finished within the --wait budget; stopped (it writes nothing)" % m)
                    else:
                        out_lines.append("--dry-run %s: exit %s" % (m, rc))
                        failed = failed or rc != 0
                    hum_lines.append(out_lines[-1])
                    out_lines.extend("  " + l for l in out.rstrip("\n").split("\n") if l)
                    trimmed = trim_gc(out, named_row, "they are in --json")
                    hum_lines.extend("  " + l for l in trimmed.rstrip("\n").split("\n") if l)
            gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "failed" if failed else "completed",
                              "report only (--dry-run; no --apply, logs and lock in a scratch dir removed after)",
                              "\n".join(out_lines), human=cap("\n".join(hum_lines)))
        elif not idn["timeout_program"]:
            gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "no timeout program (hook_timeout found neither gnutimeout nor timeout); GC not started",
                              "\n".join(notes))
        elif not state or not idn["key"]:
            gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "no state directory or stamp key; GC not started", "\n".join(notes))
        else:
            try:
                gc_run, reused, err = launch_worker(state, idn, gc_eligible, idn["timeout_program"], bgc)
            except OSError as e:
                gc_run, reused, err = None, False, "could not start the GC worker: %s" % (e.strerror or e)
            if err:
                gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", err, "\n".join(notes))
            else:
                gc_deadline = time.monotonic() + args.wait
                gc_rec = rep.step("branch-gc", "pending", ("reusing the pending worker" if reused else "worker started") + " for %d repo(s)" % len(gc_eligible),
                                  "\n".join(notes + [boundary]), result=os.path.join(gc_run, "result.json"), log=os.path.join(gc_run, "run.log"))

    # 5. Memory index.
    pool = None
    mi = sibling("memory-index")
    pool_cwd = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR") or cwd
    # The checkout hooks/memory-digest.sh passes as --ops ($OPS_DIR, else its own),
    # so the pool rebuilt here is the one the digest shows.
    ops_root = os.environ.get("OPS_DIR") or ROOT
    if not mi:
        rep.step("memory index", "failed", "memory-index not found beside session-end (%s)" % BIN)
    else:
        rc, out, err = run([mi, "--pool-for", "--cwd", pool_cwd, "--ops", ops_root], 30, merge=False)
        if rc == 0 and out.strip() and os.path.isdir(out.strip()):
            pool = out.strip()
            if dry:
                rep.step("memory index", "completed", "would rebuild %s/MEMORY.md (memory-index %s)" % (pool, pool))
            else:
                rc2, out2, _ = run([mi, pool], 120)
                if rc2 == 0:
                    rep.step("memory index", "completed", "rebuilt %s/MEMORY.md" % pool, out2)
                elif rc2 == 2:
                    rep.step("memory index", "completed", "rebuilt %s/MEMORY.md; WARNING: entries need backfill (exit 2), not a failed rebuild" % pool, out2)
                else:
                    rep.step("memory index", "failed", "memory-index %s exited %s" % (pool, rc2), out2)
        elif rc == 4:
            rep.step("memory index", "skipped", "no memory pool for %s; none created" % pool_cwd, out + err)
        else:
            rep.step("memory index", "failed", "memory-index --pool-for exited %s" % rc, out + err)

    # 6. Lint.
    gate, _ = gate_script()
    if not tx:
        rep.step("lint", "skipped", "no verified transcript, so no evidence of harness files; if this thread changed .claude-config/ or SKILLS/, run the gate's lint by hand")
    elif not harness_named:
        rep.step("lint", "skipped", "this thread named no file under .claude-config/ or SKILLS/")
    elif not gate:
        rep.step("lint", "failed", "this thread touched harness files but no gate script sits beside session-end")
    else:
        # verify-ops.sh has no lint-only mode: --quiet prints its WARN and FAIL lines
        # and the summary line, and OPS_DIR points it at this checkout, not ~/OPS.
        cmd = [gate, "--quiet"]
        env = dict(os.environ, OPS_DIR=ROOT)
        if dry:
            rep.step("lint", "completed", "would run OPS_DIR=%s %s" % (ROOT, " ".join(cmd)))
        else:
            rc, out, _ = run(cmd, 600, env=env)
            rep.step(**lint_verdict(" ".join(cmd), rc, out))

    # 4 (wait). The GC result, within the --wait budget measured from launch.
    gc_res = None
    if gc_run:
        res_path = os.path.join(gc_run, "result.json")
        lock_path = os.path.join(gc_run, "worker.lock")
        while True:
            try:
                gc_res = read_result(gc_run)
            except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
                gc_rec.update(status="failed", summary="unreadable GC result %s: %s" % (res_path, e))
                break
            if gc_res is not None:
                break
            if not lock_held(lock_path):
                try:
                    gc_res = read_result(gc_run)
                except (OSError, ValueError):
                    gc_res = None
                if gc_res is None:
                    gc_rec.update(status="failed", summary="the GC worker ended without a result; see %s/run.log" % gc_run)
                break
            left = gc_deadline - time.monotonic()
            if left <= 0:
                gc_rec.update(summary="%s; still running after the --wait budget; read %s before reporting cleanup as done (session-end finish does)"
                              % (gc_rec["summary"], res_path))
                break
            time.sleep(min(0.1, left))
        if gc_res is not None:
            ok = gc_res.get("status") == "completed"
            gc_rec.update(status="completed" if ok else "failed",
                          summary="finished: %s" % gc_res.get("status"),
                          output=(gc_rec.get("output") or "") + "\n" + "\n".join(describe_result(gc_res, gc_run)),
                          human=cap((gc_rec.get("output") or "") + "\n" + "\n".join(describe_result(gc_res, gc_run, named_row))))

    # 8 (after). Disk.
    free_after = statvfs_free()
    if free_before is None or free_after is None:
        rep.step("disk", "skipped", "statvfs / failed")
    else:
        delta = free_after - free_before
        rep.step("disk", "completed",
                 "free on /: %s before, %s after (%+.1f MiB); a box-wide observation, not bytes this thread reclaimed%s"
                 % (fmt_bytes(free_before), fmt_bytes(free_after), delta / 1024 ** 2,
                    "; GC is still running, so this sample is incomplete" if gc_rec and gc_rec["status"] == "pending" else ""),
                 "Quarantine on the same filesystem keeps a worktree's bytes.")

    # 9. Close: list what this thread created; remove nothing.
    if mode == "close":
        if not tx:
            rep.step("cleanup list", "skipped", "no verified transcript: no creation evidence to list")
        else:
            rows_by_wt = {}
            if gc_res:
                for r in gc_res["repos"]:
                    for row in r.get("rows", []):
                        wt = row[2]
                        if wt and wt != "-":
                            rows_by_wt[os.path.normpath(os.path.expanduser(wt))] = "%s: %s" % (row[4], row[5])
            roots = scratch_roots()
            owned, unknown = [], []
            for kind, name, own, how in creations(tx):
                if kind in ("file", "dir", "worktree"):
                    if kind != "worktree" and not any(under(name, r) for r in roots):
                        continue
                    if any(under(r, name) for r in roots):
                        continue  # a scratch root or its parent is never this thread's own
                    if not os.path.lexists(name):
                        continue
                    line = "%s %s (%s)" % (kind, name, how)
                    if kind == "worktree":
                        line += "; GC: %s" % rows_by_wt.get(name, "GC pending/not evaluated" if not gc_res else "no row for it")
                else:
                    pres = docker_present(kind, name)
                    if pres == "absent":
                        continue
                    line = "docker %s %s (%s; %s)" % (kind, name, how, pres)
                    if pres != "present":
                        unknown.append(line)
                        continue
                (owned if own else unknown).append(line)
            out = ["created by this thread and still present (remove by exact path or id if disposable; never over a live-worktree hold):"]
            out += ["  " + l for l in owned] or ["  (none found)"]
            if unknown:
                out.append("ownership unknown (not suggested for removal):")
                out += ["  " + l for l in unknown]
            out.append("check for anything else you created, by exact path or id; establish ownership before removing it")
            rep.step("cleanup list", "completed", "%d created object(s) listed; nothing removed" % len(owned), "\n".join(out))

    # 10. Box extras.
    # OPS ships no vault renderer, so the step is an explicit skip, never a guess.
    rep.step("vault view", "skipped", "this checkout ships no vault renderer; nothing checked or written")
    asks = sibling("asks")
    thread_for_asks = os.environ.get("ASKS_THREAD") or idn["t3_thread_id"]
    if not asks:
        rep.step("open asks", "skipped", "asks not installed on this box")
    elif not thread_for_asks:
        rep.step("open asks", "skipped", "no T3 thread id (and no ASKS_THREAD), so no register to read")
    else:
        rc, out, _ = run([asks, "list"], 30)
        rep.step("open asks", "completed" if rc == 0 else "failed", "asks list exited %s" % rc, out)

    # 11. The remainder.
    remainder(rep, mode, idn, tx, pool)

    # 7. The receipt (not on a dry run; last-closeout moves only at finish).
    status, code = rep.status()
    if not dry:
        if not state or not idn["key"]:
            rep.step("receipt", "failed", "no state directory or stamp key; no receipt written, so finish cannot run")
        else:
            try:
                d = os.path.join(state, "session-end")
                mkdirs(d)
                path = os.path.join(d, "%s.json" % idn["key"])
                status, code = rep.status()
                atomic_write(path, json.dumps({
                    "version": 1, "mode": mode, "dry_run": False, "written_at": stamp_text(),
                    "status": status, "exit": code, "identity": rep.identity,
                    "gc": {"run_dir": gc_run, "status": gc_rec["status"] if gc_rec else "skipped"},
                    "lint_findings": [l for s in rep.steps if s["step"] == "lint" and s["status"] == "findings"
                                      for l in s["fail_lines"]],
                    "steps": rep.steps}, indent=1))
                rep.receipt = path
            except OSError as e:
                rep.step("receipt", "failed", "cannot write the receipt: %s" % (e.strerror or e))
    return print_report(rep, args.json)


def remainder(rep, mode, idn, tx, pool):
    out = rep.remainder
    out.append("What only you can do now:")
    out.append("  - Save the lessons worth keeping: one fact per file in the memory pool%s. A thread with none saves none."
               % (" (%s)" % pool if pool else ""))
    out.append("  - Put knowledge where the next person will look, and fix any document this thread made untrue.")
    out.append("  - Write the resume note at the top of the anchor or baton: %s." % ", ".join(RESUME_FIELDS))
    lint = [s for s in rep.steps if s["step"] == "lint" and s["status"] == "findings"]
    if lint:
        out.append("  - Lint reported %d FAIL line(s) above: fix the ones on files this thread changed, "
                   "and name the rest as other work's in your report." % len(lint[-1]["fail_lines"]))
    # Memory stewardship: the closing agent owns it, because only it knows what this thread learned.
    if not pool:
        out.append("Memory stewardship: no pool for this directory.")
    elif not tx or not tx["first"]:
        out.append("Memory stewardship: no verified transcript window, so entries are not listed; check %s by hand." % pool)
    else:
        rows, err = entries_in_window(pool, tx["first"])
        # The pool is shared by concurrent threads, so the window list cannot say who wrote what.
        out.append("Memory stewardship (pool %s, window from %s): entries written or changed in this pool during "
                   "this thread's window, by this thread or another one sharing the pool:" % (pool, tx["first"].isoformat()))
        if err:
            out.append("  " + err)
            rep.step("memory window", "failed", err)
        else:
            out.extend(rows or ["  (no entry modified or touched in this window)"])
        out.append("  Correct an entry this thread proved wrong, merge duplicates it touched, move a lesson that belongs in a repo's docs. session-end changed no entry.")
    tid = idn["t3_thread_id"]
    if mode == "pause":
        cc = sibling("compact-cycle.sh")
        if tid and cc:
            out.append("Pause: compact with %s --target %s" % (cc, tid))
        else:
            out.append("Pause: no compact line (%s)" % ("no T3 thread id" if not tid else "compact-cycle.sh not installed"))
        out.append("  Never compact over an unanswered question.")
    elif mode == "move":
        if not os.path.isfile(KEY_SH):
            out.append("Move: key.sh not found at %s; baton path unknown" % KEY_SH)
            rep.step("baton key", "failed", "key.sh not found at %s" % KEY_SH)
        else:
            rc, key, err = run(["bash", KEY_SH], 15, cwd=idn["cwd"], merge=False)
            if rc != 0 or not key.strip():
                out.append("Move: key.sh failed (exit %s); baton path unknown" % rc)
                rep.step("baton key", "failed", "key.sh exited %s: %s" % (rc, err.strip()[:200]))
            else:
                # The SessionStart notifier (hooks/handoff-check.sh) reads
                # ${OPS_DIR:-$HOME/OPS}/.claude-handoffs; harness_home() is that directory.
                hdir = os.path.join(harness_home(), ".claude-handoffs")
                baton = os.path.join(hdir, "pending", key.strip() + ".md")
                out.append("Move: the baton is %s (%s)." % (baton, "exists: read it, never overwrite an unread one" if os.path.exists(baton) else "not written yet"))
                out.append("  One pending baton per project. Commit and push it, or the other machine never sees it.")
    elif mode == "close":
        time_block(rep, tx, idn)
        out.append("Bill only if this thread worked a ticket; read what is already on the ticket first.")
        out.append("Remove what this thread made (the cleanup list above), never another thread's.")
    finish = "session-end finish --logged N | --declined REASON" if mode == "close" else "session-end finish"
    out.append("When the above is done: %s%s" % (finish, " (N = time entries created and read back; 0 is valid)" if mode == "close" else ""))
    if mode == "close":
        out.append("Then print the receipt first, because nothing after the settle reaches the owner.")
        if tid:
            out.append("Settle: t3_thread_organize with action \"settle\" and threadId omitted, as the last tool call; it applies at turn end"
                       " (a failed turn or a queued message leaves the thread active). Only if that tool is not available: "
                       "%s settle-when-idle %s. Never both." % (sibling("t3-api.sh") or "t3-api.sh", tid))
        else:
            out.append("Settle: not a T3 thread; no settle step (see session-close teardown for tmux or a plain terminal).")


def time_block(rep, tx, idn):
    if idn["provider"] != "claude":
        rep.step("time", "skipped", UNSUPPORTED + "; no time figure")
        return
    if not tx:
        rep.step("time", "skipped", "no verified transcript; no time figure. Ask the owner for the window; never bill a guessed span.")
        return
    am = sibling("active-minutes")
    if not am:
        rep.step("time", "skipped", "active-minutes not installed on this box; no time figure")
        return
    base = tx["path"][:-len(".jsonl")]
    also = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(base), "subagents", "*.jsonl"))
                  + glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(base), "subagents", "workflows", "*", "*.jsonl")))
    also = [a for a in also if os.path.isfile(a) and not os.path.islink(a)]
    cmd = [am, tx["path"]] + (["--also"] + also if also else [])
    rc, out, _ = run(cmd, 120)
    m = re.search(r"^ACTIVE \(bill this\): ([\d.]+) min", out, re.M)
    if rc != 0 or not m:
        rep.step("time", "failed", "active-minutes exited %s%s; no time figure" % (rc, "" if m else " without an ACTIVE line"), out)
        return
    caveat = ""
    if tx["lanes"] and not also:
        caveat = ("; NOT CONFIDENT: this thread started %d lane(s) but no lane transcript exists under %s/subagents, "
                  "so gaps a lane worked through may be excluded" % (tx["lanes"], base))
    rep.step("time", "completed",
             "measured %s active minutes as evidence, not an amount to enter%s" % (m.group(1), caveat),
             out, confident=not caveat, lane_transcripts=len(also))


# --- finish ---------------------------------------------------------------------

def lock_wait():
    raw = os.environ.get("SESSION_END_LOCK_WAIT", "10")
    try:
        v = float(raw)
    except ValueError:
        v = 10.0
    return v if math.isfinite(v) and v >= 0 else 10.0


def test_hook(phase, path):
    hook = os.environ.get("SESSION_END_TEST_HOOK")
    if not hook:
        return
    rc, out, err = run([hook, phase, path], 10)
    if rc != 0:
        raise OSError("test hook %s %s exited %s: %s" % (phase, path, rc, out.strip()[:200]))


def sha256_file(path):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    size = 0
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(65536), b""):
            h.update(chunk)
            size += len(chunk)
    return size, h.hexdigest()


def archive_billing(key, outcome):
    """(ok, lines). Moves this thread's live stamps into one fresh archive
    directory, <stamp dir>/reaped/<key>-<TS>-<hex>/, each by a single rename.

    Why a rename and never a copy (a code review finding): the
    copy, compare and unlink sequence raced the stamp writers, which take no lock
    of ours; a writer that appended after the compare lost its unbilled bytes to
    the unlink while finish reported success. A rename keeps the inode, so bytes
    a writer appends through a descriptor it already holds land in the archive,
    and a writer that opens the name afterwards creates a new live file that
    stays live as fresh unbilled evidence. Nothing is deleted, so no byte can be
    lost. branch-gc's quarantine moves worktrees the same way.

    Order: the work-log first and the session-start stamp last, because the
    session-start stamp is the unbilled-window flag. A work-log that appears
    before or right after the session-start move keeps (or puts back) that flag:
    the new segment has to be reconciled first. The outcome goes into a separate
    reaped.meta written with O_EXCL after the moves, so the archived bytes stay
    exactly the stamps' own."""
    run = stamp_dir()
    reaped = os.path.join(run, "reaped")
    names = ["work-log-%s" % key, "session-start-%s" % key]
    live = [n for n in names if os.path.lexists(os.path.join(run, n))]
    if not live:
        return True, ["no live billing stamps for key %s; nothing archived (a repeated finish is a no-op)" % key]
    # Every source is checked before anything moves, so a refusal moves nothing.
    for n in live:
        src = os.path.join(run, n)
        try:
            mode = os.lstat(src).st_mode
        except FileNotFoundError:
            continue  # gone since the listing; the move loop reports it absent
        if not stat.S_ISREG(mode):
            return False, ["%s is not a regular file (a symlink or special file); nothing moved, originals left in place" % src]
    try:
        if os.path.lexists(reaped):
            if not stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(reaped).st_mode):
                return False, ["%s is not a directory (a symlink?); nothing moved, originals left in place" % reaped]
        else:
            os.mkdir(reaped, 0o700)
        adir = None
        ts = time.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%S")
        for _ in range(100):
            cand = os.path.join(reaped, "%s-%s-%s" % (key, ts, os.urandom(4).hex()))
            test_hook("archive-target", cand)
            try:
                os.mkdir(cand, 0o700)  # exclusive: an existing directory is never reused
                adir = cand
                break
            except FileExistsError:
                continue
        if adir is None:
            return False, ["no free archive directory name under %s; nothing moved" % reaped]
        fsync_dir(reaped)
    except OSError as e:
        return False, ["cannot prepare an archive directory under %s: %s; nothing moved, originals left in place" % (reaped, e)]

    moved, lines, failure = [], [], None
    wl_live = os.path.join(run, "work-log-%s" % key)
    for name in names:
        src, dest = os.path.join(run, name), os.path.join(adir, name)
        try:
            try:
                st = os.lstat(src)
            except FileNotFoundError:
                lines.append("%s: absent" % src)
                continue
            if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
                raise OSError("%s is no longer a regular file; left in place" % src)
            if name.startswith("session-start-") and os.path.lexists(wl_live):
                raise OSError("a new work-log appeared at %s during archival; session-start left live, "
                              "reconcile the new segment first" % wl_live)
            test_hook("before-move", dest)
            os.rename(src, dest)  # same filesystem by construction; never a copy
            # Record a successful move before fsync or hashing can fail: losing
            # its recovery path would strand an archived unbilled-window flag.
            moved.append((name, src, dest, None, None))
            lines.append("%s -> %s" % (src, dest))
            fsync_dir(run)
            fsync_dir(adir)
            size, digest = sha256_file(dest)
            moved[-1] = (name, src, dest, size, digest)
            test_hook("archived", src)
            if name.startswith("session-start-") and os.path.lexists(wl_live):
                # A segment arrived right after the flag moved: put the flag back
                # by link (fails rather than replace a newer live stamp).
                try:
                    os.link(dest, src)
                    os.unlink(dest)
                    moved.pop()
                    lines.pop()
                    fsync_dir(run)
                    fsync_dir(adir)
                    raise OSError("a new work-log appeared at %s during archival; session-start put back live, "
                                  "reconcile the new segment first" % wl_live)
                except FileExistsError:
                    raise OSError("a new work-log appeared at %s and a newer session-start already exists; "
                                  "the moved flag stays at %s, compare the two by hand" % (wl_live, dest))
        except OSError as e:
            failure = e
            break

    meta_ready = False
    if moved:
        meta = ["reaped_at=%s" % stamp_text(), "reaped_reason=session-end finish: %s" % outcome,
                "reaped_key=%s" % key, "status=%s" % ("partial" if failure else "complete")]
        for name, src, dest, size, digest in moved:
            meta.append("file=%s\toriginal=%s\tsize=%s\tsha256=%s" %
                        (name, src, size if size is not None else "unknown", digest or "unavailable"))
        try:
            mfd = os.open(os.path.join(adir, "reaped.meta"), os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
            with os.fdopen(mfd, "wb") as m:
                m.write(("\n".join(meta) + "\n").encode("utf-8"))
                m.flush()
                os.fsync(m.fileno())
            fsync_dir(adir)
            meta_ready = True
        except OSError as e:
            failure = failure or OSError("the stamps moved but %s/reaped.meta could not be written: %s" % (adir, e))
    else:
        try:
            os.rmdir(adir)  # this call's own empty directory
        except OSError:
            pass

    if failure:
        # A failed finish leaves its receipt active. Keep the billing window
        # discoverable too, even if the flag's rename succeeded before the
        # failure. An exclusive hard link preserves the archive and cannot
        # overwrite a newer live flag created by a writer we do not lock.
        for name, src, dest, _s, _d in moved:
            if not name.startswith("session-start-"):
                continue
            try:
                os.link(dest, src)
                fsync_dir(run)
                lines.append("billing window kept live at %s (archive preserved at %s)" % (src, dest))
            except FileExistsError:
                lines.append("live billing flag at %s was not replaced" % src)
            except OSError as e:
                lines.append("FAILED to restore the live billing flag from %s to %s: %s" % (dest, src, e))
        lines.append("FAILED: %s" % failure)
    still = [os.path.join(run, n) for n in names if os.path.lexists(os.path.join(run, n))]
    lines.append("still live: %s" % (", ".join(still) or "none"))
    if moved:
        note = ("reaped.meta holds the outcome and available sizes and sha256" if meta_ready else
                "reaped.meta could not be completed; inspect the moved files")
        lines.append("archive directory: %s (%s)" % (adir, note))
        for name, src, dest, _s, _d in moved:
            lines.append("restore %s, only while that name is free (never over a newer live stamp): mv -n %s %s" % (name, dest, src))
    return failure is None, lines


def cmd_finish(args, idn):
    rep = Report("finish", False)
    rep.identity = {k: idn[k] for k in ("provider", "session_id", "t3_thread_id", "key", "backend", "cwd")}
    state = state_dir()
    if not state or not idn["key"]:
        rep.step("receipt", "failed", "no state directory or stamp key (%s); nothing done" % (idn["key_error"] or "no gate script beside session-end"))
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    rpath = os.path.join(state, "session-end", "%s.json" % idn["key"])
    try:
        rec = read_json_strict(rpath)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        rep.step("receipt", "failed", "no receipt at %s: run session-end <pause|move|close> first" % rpath)
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        rep.step("receipt", "failed", "unreadable receipt %s: %s" % (rpath, e))
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    got = rec.get("identity") or {}
    for k in ("key", "provider", "session_id", "t3_thread_id"):
        if got.get(k) != rep.identity.get(k):
            rep.step("receipt", "failed", "the receipt at %s belongs to another thread (%s %r, this thread %r); nothing done"
                     % (rpath, k, got.get(k), rep.identity.get(k)))
            return print_report(rep, args.json)
    mode = rec.get("mode")
    if mode not in MODES or rec.get("dry_run"):
        rep.step("receipt", "failed", "the receipt at %s is not a real pause, move or close run; nothing done" % rpath)
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    if mode == "close":
        if (args.logged is None) == (args.declined is None):
            raise Usage("after a close, finish needs exactly one of --logged N or --declined REASON")
    elif args.logged is not None or args.declined is not None:
        raise Usage("--logged and --declined apply only after a close; this receipt is a %s" % mode)
    rep.mode = "finish (%s)" % mode
    if rec.get("status") == "failed":
        rep.step("receipt", "failed", "the %s run failed (%s); fix it and run session-end %s again; no stamp" % (mode, rpath, mode))
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    rep.step("receipt", "completed", "%s run of %s" % (mode, rec.get("written_at")))
    findings = rec.get("lint_findings") or []
    if findings:
        # Reported, never a refusal: whose FAIL each is was the agent's call at the start.
        rep.step("lint findings", "completed", "lint findings were reported at the start: %d" % len(findings),
                 "\n".join(findings))
    gc = rec.get("gc") or {}
    if gc.get("status") == "pending":
        rd = gc.get("run_dir") or ""
        if os.path.dirname(rd) != gc_root(state):
            rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "the receipt names an unexpected GC run directory %r" % rd)
            return print_report(rep, args.json)
        try:
            res = read_result(rd)
        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
            rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "unreadable GC result in %s: %s" % (rd, e))
            return print_report(rep, args.json)
        if res is None:
            if lock_held(os.path.join(rd, "worker.lock")):
                rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "GC is still running (%s); run finish again once %s/result.json exists; no stamp" % (rd, rd))
            else:
                rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "the GC worker ended without a result; see %s/run.log; no stamp" % rd)
            return print_report(rep, args.json)
        if res.get("status") != "completed":
            rep.step("branch-gc", "failed", "GC finished with a failure; no stamp", "\n".join(describe_result(res, rd)),
                     human="\n".join(describe_result(res, rd, row_namer(None, set()))))
            return print_report(rep, args.json)
        rep.step("branch-gc", "completed", "the pending GC run finished cleanly", "\n".join(describe_result(res, rd)),
                 human="\n".join(describe_result(res, rd, row_namer(None, set()))))
    if mode == "close":
        if args.logged is not None:
            outcome = "logged=%s time entries created and read back" % args.logged
        else:
            outcome = "declined: %s" % args.declined
        why = billing_key_ok(idn)
        if why and idn["provider"] != "claude":
            rep.step("billing stamps", "skipped", why)
        elif why:
            rep.step("billing stamps", "failed", why + "; originals left in place; no stamp")
            return print_report(rep, args.json)
        else:
            ok, lines = archive_billing(idn["key"], outcome)
            rep.step("billing stamps", "completed" if ok else "failed",
                     "%s: %s" % ("recorded outcome" if ok else "archive failed for outcome", outcome), "\n".join(lines))
            if not ok:
                return print_report(rep, args.json)
    try:
        atomic_write(os.path.join(state, "last-closeout"), stamp_text() + "\n", mode=0o644)
        done = os.path.join(state, "session-end", "done")
        mkdirs(done)
        os.replace(rpath, os.path.join(done, "%s-%s.json" % (idn["key"], time.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%S"))))
    except OSError as e:
        rep.step("closeout stamp", "failed", "cannot write %s/last-closeout or retire the receipt: %s" % (state, e.strerror or e))
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    rep.step("closeout stamp", "completed", "advanced %s/last-closeout; receipt moved to %s" % (state, done))
    return print_report(rep, args.json)


def run_ending(args):
    """Serialize the entire read/act/retire cycle per receipt key. Locking just
    archive_billing let an overlapping start replace the receipt a finish then
    retired, and let two starts both launch a worker before either set the run
    pointer. The lock must cover the receipt read through its retirement."""
    idn = identity(os.getcwd())
    if args.cmd == "end" and args.dry_run:
        return cmd_end(args, idn)
    rep = Report("finish" if args.cmd == "finish" else args.mode, False)
    rep.identity = {k: idn[k] for k in ("provider", "session_id", "t3_thread_id", "key", "backend", "cwd")}
    why = lane_refusal()
    if why:
        rep.step("lane check", "failed", why)
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    state = state_dir()
    if not state or not idn["key"]:
        rep.step("receipt", "failed", "no state directory or stamp key (%s); nothing done" %
                 (idn["key_error"] or "no gate script beside session-end"))
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    try:
        lock_dir = os.path.join(state, "session-end", "locks")
        mkdirs(lock_dir)
        lfd = os.open(os.path.join(lock_dir, "billing-%s.lock" % idn["key"]),
                      os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
    except OSError as e:
        rep.step("receipt lock", "failed", "cannot acquire the receipt/billing lock: %s; nothing done" % e)
        return print_report(rep, args.json)
    try:
        end = time.monotonic() + lock_wait()
        while True:
            try:
                fcntl.flock(lfd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                break
            except BlockingIOError:
                if time.monotonic() >= end:
                    rep.step("receipt lock", "failed", "another ending for this key holds the billing lock; nothing done")
                    return print_report(rep, args.json)
                time.sleep(min(0.1, max(0, end - time.monotonic())))
        return cmd_finish(args, idn) if args.cmd == "finish" else cmd_end(args, idn)
    finally:
        os.close(lfd)


# --- arguments ------------------------------------------------------------------

class Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):
    def error(self, message):
        raise Usage(message)


def wait_seconds(v):
    try:
        f = float(v)
    except ValueError:
        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError("--wait takes seconds, got %r" % v)
    if not math.isfinite(f) or f < 0:
        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError("--wait takes a finite nonnegative number of seconds, got %r" % v)
    return f


def logged_count(v):
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", v or ""):
        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError("--logged takes a nonnegative whole number of time entries, got %r" % v)
    return int(v)


def reason_text(v):
    v = (v or "").strip()
    if not v or any(ord(ch) < 32 for ch in v):
        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError("--declined needs a nonempty one-line reason")
    return v


def parse(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["finish"]:
        p = Parser(prog="session-end finish", description="Finish an ending after knowledge capture (see the header).")
        g = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
        g.add_argument("--logged", type=logged_count, metavar="N")
        g.add_argument("--declined", type=reason_text, metavar="REASON")
        p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
        a = p.parse_args(argv[1:])
        a.cmd = "finish"
        return a
    p = Parser(prog="session-end", description="The mechanical half of ending a thread (see the header). "
               "Also: session-end finish [--logged N | --declined REASON] [--json].")
    p.add_argument("mode", choices=MODES)
    p.add_argument("--repo", action="append", default=[], metavar="PATH")
    p.add_argument("--transcript", metavar="FILE")
    p.add_argument("--wait", type=wait_seconds, default=90.0, metavar="SECONDS")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    a = p.parse_args(argv)
    a.cmd = "end"
    return a


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["_gc-worker"] and len(argv) == 3:
        return gc_worker(argv[1], int(argv[2]))
    if argv[:1] in (["-h"], ["--help"]):
        print(__doc__)
        return 0
    try:
        args = parse(argv)
        return run_ending(args)
    except Usage as e:
        sys.stderr.write("session-end: %s\n(session-end <pause|move|close> [--repo PATH]... [--transcript FILE] "
                         "[--wait SECONDS] [--dry-run] [--json] | session-end finish [--logged N | --declined REASON] [--json])\n" % e)
        return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
